cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its study records, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Telohelm on ArduPilot: code, protocols and analysis for \"Code that never ran: testing and repairing flight procedures that a language model writes for ArduPilot in simulation\""
abstract: >-
  Telohelm has a language model write a short Python procedure that flies a
  multirotor under the ArduPilot autopilot in simulation, and a monitor adopts
  the procedure only if it meets its goal on every test flight. This
  repository holds the code as each of the paper's two studies flew it, the
  protocols fixed before each study, the validation check, the analysis and an
  independent recomputation of the main results. A script checks the paper's
  results from the study records, which are archived with it on Zenodo.
